VF31 passes ar-cs-possession at last, and a correct read was losing to the stale one it replaced\n\nPASS_COMPLETE_INDEPENDENT: fifteen obligations, all measurable, all PASS, none\nNOT_MEASURABLE_HERE. The digests never moved and VF31 pinned that harder than FIX01 did\n-- fixtures/ is still tree e43c0ffb32c6d5734bca3446b702722927230e0e, spanning 113 commits\non HEAD's ancestry rather than the four FIX01 claimed for it.\n\nThe petition's boundary caption is untouched more strongly than FIX01 said: the two\nrendered arrays are IDENTICAL, maxAbsGreyDiff 0 and pixelsWithAnyGreyDiff 0 of 2,103,750,\nso the zero holds at every possible threshold rather than the six swept. It renders\nidentically not because the fill was skipped but because all 70 widgets are flattened in\nevery fixture, and a refused blank's flattened appearance reproduces the source's empty\none exactly. The seven refusals confirm three independent ways, including a per-widget\nraster over all 70 rects in all four fixtures with zero anomalies.\n\nAND THE VERDICT WAS BEING DISCARDED. The extractor read this PASS as declaring no base,\nso it lost supersession to the same lane's older FAIL, which did carry a per-row one. A\ncorrect later read was losing to the stale read it replaced.\n\nThe cause is a rule that is right, applied where its hazard cannot arise. The extractor\nrefuses to inherit a document-level base because files appended to by successive lanes\nwould stamp a later team's baseSha onto older rows -- that is how a stale vf11 FAIL came\nto wear a fresh base. But that needs more than one lane in the file. VF31 wrote a\nsingle-lane file declaring lane, laneKind and one verifiedAtBase at the top, so its rows\ncarried none of their own.\n\nMeasured before changing it: of 313 row files, 61 carry a document-level base with at\nleast one row lacking one. 50 declare a single lane with every row belonging to it, where\nthe hazard cannot arise; 11 are multi-lane or name no lane, and those keep the refusal.\nThe inheritance is now allowed exactly where the file proves it is safe -- the document\nnames a lane and no row names a different one.\n\nI checked the blast radius rather than trusting the reasoning: exactly one family's state\nmoved, the intended one. FAIL_REPAIR_REQUIRED -> BUILT_RASTER_PENDING, and it owes the\ncentral raster its earlier receipt no longer covers.\n\nTHE GUARD HAS A HOLE ITS AUTHOR DID NOT REPORT. VF31 extracted both guards verbatim --\nhaving to extend its own brace-matcher for a regex literal containing a bracket and a\nquote -- and reproduced FIX01's claim exactly against the prior commit: 6 contradictions,\n7 undisclosed pairs. But it built its own mutation battery rather than reusing FIX01's\ntwelve, which are recorded NOWHERE in the committed tree, so that strength evidence\ncannot be re-derived by anyone. Of its own: 7 refused, 8 passed, five of the passes real\nblind spots and one sharp -- inverting step 10 from \"write in by hand any that arrived\nempty\" to \"assume they are correct if they arrived empty\" PASSES BOTH GUARDS. That is\nthe same defect class FIX01 found by hand in old line 16: the guard catches \"this blank\nis filled\" and cannot catch \"do nothing about this blank being empty\".\n\nAND A FIFTH BLANK NOBODY HAD COUNTED. Each caption has five blanks, not three: IN THE and\nDIVISION are decision=refuse on both documents and the packet never attempts them. Step 4\ntells the petition's participant the caption \"is already filled in\" and offers \"arrived\nempty\" as the only reason a blank could be empty -- the wrong explanation for two blanks\nthat are empty by design. The consistency guard structurally cannot see it, because its\nanchors come only from refusable.map(r => r.field) and a never-written blank has no\nanchor. VF31 demonstrated it: \"The court name is already filled in on the petition and on\nthe order\" passes both guards. The packet recovers in four other places, so it recorded\nit rather than failing on it.\n\nOne correction to my own record, which I will fix separately: REFUSAL_CLAIMS_NOTHING_WAS_\nWRITTEN.json is stale for this builder now, and its firstWriteAtLine 404 points at the\nwriteJson HELPER DEFINITION rather than a call, which is why it reads 25 of 25.\n\nTerminal holds at 200 of 346; every step exited 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W3FAJNotS5DdvyJS1khjid","timestamp":"2026-09-10T10:14:33Z","author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"}},"repository":{"id":1248656766,"node_id":"R_kgDOSmz9fg","name":"legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","full_name":"Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","private":false,"owner":{"login":"Roger-LegalEase","id":287531360,"node_id":"U_kgDOESNhYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287531360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase","html_url":"https://github.com/Roger-LegalEase","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","description":null,"fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-cl